<title>FRANCE: U.S. main origin for Paris May imports.</title>
<headline>U.S. main origin for Paris May imports.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>The United States was the principal country of origin for import traffic handled at the Paris airports in May 1997, Aeroports de Paris (ADP) said.</p>
<p>May import traffic to the Paris airports, Charles de Gaulle and Orly, totalled 42,443 tonnes, an increase of 4.1 percent on the same month last year.</p>
<p>The top 20 countries of origin for ADP imports in May, with percentage change on May 1996, were:</p>
<p>    Origin		tonnes     Percent</p>
<p>					   Change 1996</p>
<p>    1. United States  11,359     down   5.0</p>
<p>    2. India	     1,977     down   6.3</p>
<p>    3. UK		  1,959	 up  30.2</p>
<p>    4. Canada	    1,881     down  19.9</p>
<p>    5. Japan	     1,836	 up  24.5</p>
<p>    6. Hong Kong	 1,516	 up  17.6</p>
<p>    7. Germany	   1,306	 up   3.7</p>
<p>    8. Italy	     1,054     down   9.7</p>
<p>    9. Thailand	  1,022	 up  16.6</p>
<p>   10. Singapore	   758	 up 142.5</p>
<p>   11. Kenya		 708     down  18.9</p>
<p>   12. China		 657	 up  90.7</p>
<p>   13. Egypt		 637	 up  66.2</p>
<p>   14. Taiwan		633	 up  46.9</p>
<p>   15. Mauritius	   560	 up  38.6</p>
<p>   17. South Africa	522     down   1.2</p>
<p>   18. Fr. West Indies   519	 up   6.8</p>
<p>   19. Korea		 484	 up   1.9</p>
<p>   20. Brazil		466	 up  14.0</p>
